[{:db/id 17592186162123 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3339efa3-bc24-59b5-979e-3e7acd556435" "question-ce8c7ab6-3d50-5c46-82fd-86a6317c7440" "question-939333b2-51e3-5bb6-8750-03bc60fa06d3" "question-a9fb15b7-a2f0-5eaf-82a8-f09127855863" "question-f28e401e-edf5-5575-9abc-2915f050b3a4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161689 :question/problem "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 2)$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ |\n\nFind the $\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=2\\big]$ given that the conditional probability mass function $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 2)$ is shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=x\\big] = \\sum_{y} y \\, f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162126 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-26cf687b-fdce-54b3-aa67-a91fa8446cfe" "question-140a6023-d1bd-5fed-ac27-734185236cc4" "question-bb7f31f7-87d5-5229-8b2b-b9942d154a36" "question-39351ca5-4e9c-5435-bca1-f99ac80dd168"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161692 :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=2\\big]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=x\\big] = \\sum_{y} y \\, f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $f_X(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{13}{27}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\nf_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x)  = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_X(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x{:}$\n\n| $f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{13}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{13}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{8}{13}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162133 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-772539cc-05a8-509a-9c28-5f9d52c588ed" "question-5f79f694-778f-5d59-a788-db878bd2c81e" "question-d4b4bf79-088a-5fc8-9216-d79eb330f015" "question-8aa088c8-e9f1-58c7-81a8-b2d5b673243c" "question-a956b539-c977-51d6-9b04-f769aaa2a1a8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161699 :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\textrm{E}\\big[X \\,|\\, Y=1\\big]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[X \\,|\\, Y=y\\big] = \\sum_{x} x \\, f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $\\dfrac{5}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{4}{9}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\nf_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y)  = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_Y(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y{:}$\n\n| $f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}+4\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{5} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-3339efa3-bc24-59b5-979e-3e7acd556435" :question/id #uuid "3339efa3-bc24-59b5-979e-3e7acd556435" :question/math-academy-id "q-146184" :question/problem "| $x$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |\n\nFind the $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)$ is shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=0] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+5\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d1d31ba-190a-58c9-9a39-b1445a487d80"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d1d31ba-190a-58c9-9a39-b1445a487d80" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d1d31ba-190a-58c9-9a39-b1445a487d80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4805957f-3e58-5699-b156-c74126f89c27" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4805957f-3e58-5699-b156-c74126f89c27" "answer-c2bb301a-985f-5815-8a2b-bec7a9094a3f" "answer-81ce082c-a8e9-5aec-a1e9-a43a2df3f377" "answer-40f65c56-6f14-5664-8e36-9a21f64f5b94" "answer-669f32a5-42f7-5f36-bed2-8ba0c15fb5dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4805957f-3e58-5699-b156-c74126f89c27" :answer/id #uuid "4805957f-3e58-5699-b156-c74126f89c27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2bb301a-985f-5815-8a2b-bec7a9094a3f" :answer/id #uuid "c2bb301a-985f-5815-8a2b-bec7a9094a3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81ce082c-a8e9-5aec-a1e9-a43a2df3f377" :answer/id #uuid "81ce082c-a8e9-5aec-a1e9-a43a2df3f377" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40f65c56-6f14-5664-8e36-9a21f64f5b94" :answer/id #uuid "40f65c56-6f14-5664-8e36-9a21f64f5b94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-669f32a5-42f7-5f36-bed2-8ba0c15fb5dc" :answer/id #uuid "669f32a5-42f7-5f36-bed2-8ba0c15fb5dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ce8c7ab6-3d50-5c46-82fd-86a6317c7440" :question/id #uuid "ce8c7ab6-3d50-5c46-82fd-86a6317c7440" :question/math-academy-id "q-146190" :question/problem "| $y$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ | $0.25$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ |\n\nFind the $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=3]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ is shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=3] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.25+3\\cdot 0.6+5\\cdot 0.15 \\\\  & =3.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ada42878-28c7-51a7-9c8d-0a81ac88a20f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ada42878-28c7-51a7-9c8d-0a81ac88a20f" :answer-field/id #uuid "ada42878-28c7-51a7-9c8d-0a81ac88a20f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-08a6111f-b56b-5e44-9927-b6464728bb0a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-85bb055b-e38e-5b00-90bc-b8ab2dd1d129" "answer-1ae44c12-040b-59bb-ac20-ee680c8d7ad0" "answer-08a6111f-b56b-5e44-9927-b6464728bb0a" "answer-8eb6531d-a864-5261-aeb8-0bf3307ad32d" "answer-9e1414fa-4702-5667-8953-c2e463f92750"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85bb055b-e38e-5b00-90bc-b8ab2dd1d129" :answer/id #uuid "85bb055b-e38e-5b00-90bc-b8ab2dd1d129" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.85" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ae44c12-040b-59bb-ac20-ee680c8d7ad0" :answer/id #uuid "1ae44c12-040b-59bb-ac20-ee680c8d7ad0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08a6111f-b56b-5e44-9927-b6464728bb0a" :answer/id #uuid "08a6111f-b56b-5e44-9927-b6464728bb0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8eb6531d-a864-5261-aeb8-0bf3307ad32d" :answer/id #uuid "8eb6531d-a864-5261-aeb8-0bf3307ad32d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.55" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e1414fa-4702-5667-8953-c2e463f92750" :answer/id #uuid "9e1414fa-4702-5667-8953-c2e463f92750" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-939333b2-51e3-5bb6-8750-03bc60fa06d3" :question/id #uuid "939333b2-51e3-5bb6-8750-03bc60fa06d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-146178" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.4, & \\,x=2 \\\\ 0.6, & \\,x=4 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.4+4\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =3.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ee551253-7ac7-5893-8b62-119334eeaa4e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ee551253-7ac7-5893-8b62-119334eeaa4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee551253-7ac7-5893-8b62-119334eeaa4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e6f9876c-7457-52bd-9550-982c85fc3c11" :answer-field/choices ["answer-04d3bd28-c2f2-5491-924f-6e0c82e09fc1" "answer-154651d3-01b5-5743-b141-561396010474" "answer-e6f9876c-7457-52bd-9550-982c85fc3c11" "answer-8ff28f86-1d55-510a-9cd6-eb4be7a1436e" "answer-42dcc74d-758e-5042-9242-b5eb9bfe4e31"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04d3bd28-c2f2-5491-924f-6e0c82e09fc1" :answer/id #uuid "04d3bd28-c2f2-5491-924f-6e0c82e09fc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-154651d3-01b5-5743-b141-561396010474" :answer/id #uuid "154651d3-01b5-5743-b141-561396010474" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6f9876c-7457-52bd-9550-982c85fc3c11" :answer/id #uuid "e6f9876c-7457-52bd-9550-982c85fc3c11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ff28f86-1d55-510a-9cd6-eb4be7a1436e" :answer/id #uuid "8ff28f86-1d55-510a-9cd6-eb4be7a1436e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42dcc74d-758e-5042-9242-b5eb9bfe4e31" :answer/id #uuid "42dcc74d-758e-5042-9242-b5eb9bfe4e31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a9fb15b7-a2f0-5eaf-82a8-f09127855863" :question/id #uuid "a9fb15b7-a2f0-5eaf-82a8-f09127855863" :question/math-academy-id "q-146186" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.3, & \\,x=3 \\\\ 0.7, & \\,x=5 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=2] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0.3+5\\cdot 0.7 \\\\  & =4.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b303c7aa-5c57-574c-b73d-694f3cc1bba8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b303c7aa-5c57-574c-b73d-694f3cc1bba8" :answer-field/id #uuid "b303c7aa-5c57-574c-b73d-694f3cc1bba8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-80fe22d6-3fa3-550b-9553-fd0c562a0c4d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18750022-8351-5a3e-ae1c-0ae0a5ecd278" "answer-2b9b402d-5456-5fb4-85a4-bc43a48af4ad" "answer-80fe22d6-3fa3-550b-9553-fd0c562a0c4d" "answer-012ca9e0-686a-5d19-b689-9cff442f5919" "answer-ebef240d-f4fa-5c98-be54-34edb0d5f4c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18750022-8351-5a3e-ae1c-0ae0a5ecd278" :answer/id #uuid "18750022-8351-5a3e-ae1c-0ae0a5ecd278" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b9b402d-5456-5fb4-85a4-bc43a48af4ad" :answer/id #uuid "2b9b402d-5456-5fb4-85a4-bc43a48af4ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80fe22d6-3fa3-550b-9553-fd0c562a0c4d" :answer/id #uuid "80fe22d6-3fa3-550b-9553-fd0c562a0c4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-012ca9e0-686a-5d19-b689-9cff442f5919" :answer/id #uuid "012ca9e0-686a-5d19-b689-9cff442f5919" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebef240d-f4fa-5c98-be54-34edb0d5f4c1" :answer/id #uuid "ebef240d-f4fa-5c98-be54-34edb0d5f4c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f28e401e-edf5-5575-9abc-2915f050b3a4" :question/id #uuid "f28e401e-edf5-5575-9abc-2915f050b3a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-146195" :question/problem "| $y$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6)$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |\n\nFind the $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=6]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6)$ is shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=6] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}+4\\cdot \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-da6775a2-3477-5814-8673-a2afece275be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-da6775a2-3477-5814-8673-a2afece275be" :answer-field/id #uuid "da6775a2-3477-5814-8673-a2afece275be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-24bd83e9-4aca-5cee-8abb-c5ef79d6f231" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3489b1cd-aa26-5482-95b3-77d7b787acf9" "answer-860cc4fb-2f2e-5c43-99d8-5e61965e83a6" "answer-24bd83e9-4aca-5cee-8abb-c5ef79d6f231" "answer-8fcfaa63-b43e-5f80-9493-71e97f97f080" "answer-41821c99-6149-54f3-ac01-33b1080a57f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3489b1cd-aa26-5482-95b3-77d7b787acf9" :answer/id #uuid "3489b1cd-aa26-5482-95b3-77d7b787acf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-860cc4fb-2f2e-5c43-99d8-5e61965e83a6" :answer/id #uuid "860cc4fb-2f2e-5c43-99d8-5e61965e83a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24bd83e9-4aca-5cee-8abb-c5ef79d6f231" :answer/id #uuid "24bd83e9-4aca-5cee-8abb-c5ef79d6f231" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fcfaa63-b43e-5f80-9493-71e97f97f080" :answer/id #uuid "8fcfaa63-b43e-5f80-9493-71e97f97f080" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41821c99-6149-54f3-ac01-33b1080a57f7" :answer/id #uuid "41821c99-6149-54f3-ac01-33b1080a57f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162428 :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{3}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{3}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159770 :answer-field/correct 17592186159773 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-26cf687b-fdce-54b3-aa67-a91fa8446cfe" :question/id #uuid "26cf687b-fdce-54b3-aa67-a91fa8446cfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-146231" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+1+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-835c9abf-c451-5b78-b156-3604c5d60e7c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-835c9abf-c451-5b78-b156-3604c5d60e7c" :answer-field/id #uuid "835c9abf-c451-5b78-b156-3604c5d60e7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6d6b8fe8-56f9-59aa-8b89-fe1537ab4b01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-faec11ff-711a-5f97-839f-60ad7bc32805" "answer-a028479d-d79f-5a1c-9d56-22c577bb86aa" "answer-ee2c88ed-6294-5eab-8b70-7693a739d009" "answer-6d6b8fe8-56f9-59aa-8b89-fe1537ab4b01" "answer-931b6f66-e009-56b0-84c9-c7b511351fcb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-faec11ff-711a-5f97-839f-60ad7bc32805" :answer/id #uuid "faec11ff-711a-5f97-839f-60ad7bc32805" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a028479d-d79f-5a1c-9d56-22c577bb86aa" :answer/id #uuid "a028479d-d79f-5a1c-9d56-22c577bb86aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee2c88ed-6294-5eab-8b70-7693a739d009" :answer/id #uuid "ee2c88ed-6294-5eab-8b70-7693a739d009" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d6b8fe8-56f9-59aa-8b89-fe1537ab4b01" :answer/id #uuid "6d6b8fe8-56f9-59aa-8b89-fe1537ab4b01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-931b6f66-e009-56b0-84c9-c7b511351fcb" :answer/id #uuid "931b6f66-e009-56b0-84c9-c7b511351fcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-140a6023-d1bd-5fed-ac27-734185236cc4" :question/id #uuid "140a6023-d1bd-5fed-ac27-734185236cc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-146243" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=0]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=0] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+2\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fb992380-62f1-562c-8eda-7def00bd1a46"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fb992380-62f1-562c-8eda-7def00bd1a46" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb992380-62f1-562c-8eda-7def00bd1a46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3f535cc8-b1c1-5320-aa7c-2bb3717ae519" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b25405f2-5401-55f8-bb8b-3f8bf7ab02cb" "answer-5113d4f2-d040-55bb-8718-e7866220b1a0" "answer-3f535cc8-b1c1-5320-aa7c-2bb3717ae519" "answer-3e57c085-bef8-5b19-96ef-660405e46e23" "answer-751bca34-df20-599a-ba4a-2a74babb6229"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b25405f2-5401-55f8-bb8b-3f8bf7ab02cb" :answer/id #uuid "b25405f2-5401-55f8-bb8b-3f8bf7ab02cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5113d4f2-d040-55bb-8718-e7866220b1a0" :answer/id #uuid "5113d4f2-d040-55bb-8718-e7866220b1a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f535cc8-b1c1-5320-aa7c-2bb3717ae519" :answer/id #uuid "3f535cc8-b1c1-5320-aa7c-2bb3717ae519" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e57c085-bef8-5b19-96ef-660405e46e23" :answer/id #uuid "3e57c085-bef8-5b19-96ef-660405e46e23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-751bca34-df20-599a-ba4a-2a74babb6229" :answer/id #uuid "751bca34-df20-599a-ba4a-2a74babb6229" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bb7f31f7-87d5-5229-8b2b-b9942d154a36" :question/id #uuid "bb7f31f7-87d5-5229-8b2b-b9942d154a36" :question/math-academy-id "q-146228" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=4]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ |\n| $X=16$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ | $\\frac{4}{7}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=4] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{3}{7}+2\\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-850ee2d1-bd49-535c-a62b-43d34186ea0e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-850ee2d1-bd49-535c-a62b-43d34186ea0e" :answer-field/id #uuid "850ee2d1-bd49-535c-a62b-43d34186ea0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b43612d7-bf1e-5f84-8191-a06a292f68a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b77fd82b-b377-58e7-a765-bf80768a969f" "answer-b43612d7-bf1e-5f84-8191-a06a292f68a4" "answer-8a1066f7-bb78-5f0e-aff8-c601e183c200" "answer-ca63eb7e-3b07-5c85-9289-17dcbe19c2ca" "answer-203a2e87-3d58-5bc6-b6d1-0a9a3a5e40e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b77fd82b-b377-58e7-a765-bf80768a969f" :answer/id #uuid "b77fd82b-b377-58e7-a765-bf80768a969f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b43612d7-bf1e-5f84-8191-a06a292f68a4" :answer/id #uuid "b43612d7-bf1e-5f84-8191-a06a292f68a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a1066f7-bb78-5f0e-aff8-c601e183c200" :answer/id #uuid "8a1066f7-bb78-5f0e-aff8-c601e183c200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca63eb7e-3b07-5c85-9289-17dcbe19c2ca" :answer/id #uuid "ca63eb7e-3b07-5c85-9289-17dcbe19c2ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-203a2e87-3d58-5bc6-b6d1-0a9a3a5e40e2" :answer/id #uuid "203a2e87-3d58-5bc6-b6d1-0a9a3a5e40e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-39351ca5-4e9c-5435-bca1-f99ac80dd168" :question/id #uuid "39351ca5-4e9c-5435-bca1-f99ac80dd168" :question/math-academy-id "q-146217" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b446a07a-b5b0-5499-8e0d-3c17c2bc8605"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b446a07a-b5b0-5499-8e0d-3c17c2bc8605" :answer-field/id #uuid "b446a07a-b5b0-5499-8e0d-3c17c2bc8605" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b4b5981e-4b33-59a8-8753-4b483d248538" :answer-field/choices ["a