$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ | $\\frac{5}{9}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=5] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,5) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}+3\\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-af90d537-2226-55dc-b3c7-825175a82cc4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-af90d537-2226-55dc-b3c7-825175a82cc4" :answer-field/id #uuid "af90d537-2226-55dc-b3c7-825175a82cc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3a42be61-22c5-534f-8367-1f2b6a83efcd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-29ce2577-7b12-5b69-bf4f-e7ef0beae6fb" "answer-d933d782-b1ae-598e-96f1-84f2b07f3337" "answer-3a42be61-22c5-534f-8367-1f2b6a83efcd" "answer-c275e15d-7427-5179-9ff7-1b9970ae80ae" "answer-89662e88-e4b9-5dff-908a-c5a610a568d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29ce2577-7b12-5b69-bf4f-e7ef0beae6fb" :answer/id #uuid "29ce2577-7b12-5b69-bf4f-e7ef0beae6fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d933d782-b1ae-598e-96f1-84f2b07f3337" :answer/id #uuid "d933d782-b1ae-598e-96f1-84f2b07f3337" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a42be61-22c5-534f-8367-1f2b6a83efcd" :answer/id #uuid "3a42be61-22c5-534f-8367-1f2b6a83efcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c275e15d-7427-5179-9ff7-1b9970ae80ae" :answer/id #uuid "c275e15d-7427-5179-9ff7-1b9970ae80ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89662e88-e4b9-5dff-908a-c5a610a568d6" :answer/id #uuid "89662e88-e4b9-5dff-908a-c5a610a568d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f79f694-778f-5d59-a788-db878bd2c81e" :question/id #uuid "5f79f694-778f-5d59-a788-db878bd2c81e" :question/math-academy-id "q-146269" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{5}{12}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{5}{12}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{23}{36}$ | $\\frac{13}{36}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{6}{23}$ | $\\frac{3}{13}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{15}{23}$ | $\\frac{6}{13}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{2}{23}$ | $\\frac{4}{13}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{3}{13}+2\\cdot \\frac{6}{13}+3\\cdot \\frac{4}{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-79907d47-1504-5e91-bf3a-7e83b5cf4a38"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-79907d47-1504-5e91-bf3a-7e83b5cf4a38" :answer-field/id #uuid "79907d47-1504-5e91-bf3a-7e83b5cf4a38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4a003ac7-9d7e-557a-a545-ad6ec63a5035" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1991bab4-49b8-54dd-b4f6-f2270e903d54" "answer-8f463d0f-88db-5888-87fa-99da129c4406" "answer-4a003ac7-9d7e-557a-a545-ad6ec63a5035" "answer-e23a8846-4f4a-5ed8-8760-2d5add78477f" "answer-0b7f7bee-bbb0-5712-93eb-4602e11471f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1991bab4-49b8-54dd-b4f6-f2270e903d54" :answer/id #uuid "1991bab4-49b8-54dd-b4f6-f2270e903d54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f463d0f-88db-5888-87fa-99da129c4406" :answer/id #uuid "8f463d0f-88db-5888-87fa-99da129c4406" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a003ac7-9d7e-557a-a545-ad6ec63a5035" :answer/id #uuid "4a003ac7-9d7e-557a-a545-ad6ec63a5035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e23a8846-4f4a-5ed8-8760-2d5add78477f" :answer/id #uuid "e23a8846-4f4a-5ed8-8760-2d5add78477f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{23}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b7f7bee-bbb0-5712-93eb-4602e11471f5" :answer/id #uuid "0b7f7bee-bbb0-5712-93eb-4602e11471f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{31}{23}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d4b4bf79-088a-5fc8-9216-d79eb330f015" :question/id #uuid "d4b4bf79-088a-5fc8-9216-d79eb330f015" :question/math-academy-id "q-146285" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| $X=5$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=5]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| $X=5$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=5$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=5] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,5) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f8b2222a-a8b2-53ca-a03a-b94a200b38c9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f8b2222a-a8b2-53ca-a03a-b94a200b38c9" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8b2222a-a8b2-53ca-a03a-b94a200b38c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9476e763-4c3c-54c6-a0c8-076e92e15e0f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9476e763-4c3c-54c6-a0c8-076e92e15e0f" "answer-fda16633-07f3-5c38-b3b7-2e49f834df6d" "answer-1efd0d99-8bf2-51e6-9811-f57601cb3164" "answer-24080fff-d155-550a-9fea-c2aa82e94ae7" "answer-f27ea431-e80b-53d4-9c3a-bd97a2ed2813"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9476e763-4c3c-54c6-a0c8-076e92e15e0f" :answer/id #uuid "9476e763-4c3c-54c6-a0c8-076e92e15e0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fda16633-07f3-5c38-b3b7-2e49f834df6d" :answer/id #uuid "fda16633-07f3-5c38-b3b7-2e49f834df6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1efd0d99-8bf2-51e6-9811-f57601cb3164" :answer/id #uuid "1efd0d99-8bf2-51e6-9811-f57601cb3164" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24080fff-d155-550a-9fea-c2aa82e94ae7" :answer/id #uuid "24080fff-d155-550a-9fea-c2aa82e94ae7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f27ea431-e80b-53d4-9c3a-bd97a2ed2813" :answer/id #uuid "f27ea431-e80b-53d4-9c3a-bd97a2ed2813" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8aa088c8-e9f1-58c7-81a8-b2d5b673243c" :question/id #uuid "8aa088c8-e9f1-58c7-81a8-b2d5b673243c" :question/math-academy-id "q-146273" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{5}{27}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{5}{27}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{17}{27}$ | $\\frac{10}{27}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{3}{17}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{9}{17}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{5}{17}$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{3}{10}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}+3\\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ddbbb6b1-d3fb-55d3-9d3f-866654dc76c0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ddbbb6b1-d3fb-55d3-9d3f-866654dc76c0" :answer-field/id #uuid "ddbbb6b1-d3fb-55d3-9d3f-866654dc76c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5090b2a9-387a-54aa-9b1e-641e511dd5dd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-850d7772-eb78-5b12-9250-109f9ce8268a" "answer-ba410149-bfd2-57c3-88d6-f4378e3f5776" "answer-c445a323-da65-56bf-92cb-33fca15466a3" "answer-5090b2a9-387a-54aa-9b1e-641e511dd5dd" "answer-24fc62b0-3dba-54e8-b983-afdecb5c2cdb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-850d7772-eb78-5b12-9250-109f9ce8268a" :answer/id #uuid "850d7772-eb78-5b12-9250-109f9ce8268a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba410149-bfd2-57c3-88d6-f4378e3f5776" :answer/id #uuid "ba410149-bfd2-57c3-88d6-f4378e3f5776" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c445a323-da65-56bf-92cb-33fca15466a3" :answer/id #uuid "c445a323-da65-56bf-92cb-33fca15466a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5090b2a9-387a-54aa-9b1e-641e511dd5dd" :answer/id #uuid "5090b2a9-387a-54aa-9b1e-641e511dd5dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24fc62b0-3dba-54e8-b983-afdecb5c2cdb" :answer/id #uuid "24fc62b0-3dba-54e8-b983-afdecb5c2cdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a956b539-c977-51d6-9b04-f769aaa2a1a8" :question/id #uuid "a956b539-c977-51d6-9b04-f769aaa2a1a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-146286" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=5$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=5$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{7}{10}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=5$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{4}{7}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=0] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0209e7c1-5b71-52a4-b949-2b70cb41a46a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0209e7c1-5b71-52a4-b949-2b70cb41a46a" :answer-field/id #uuid "0209e7c1-5b71-52a4-b949-2b70cb41a46a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-84aa4f2d-de88-5e30-8118-904ad76280e3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4d4542b-e41d-5aa5-b77f-61338768d4ed" "answer-d5aa0e64-7998-506a-b005-217cd2d97fd9" "answer-84aa4f2d-de88-5e30-8118-904ad76280e3" "answer-19f056e4-3325-5f66-8071-2407f11d4bc8" "answer-3a1fe014-940d-5195-b2a9-07750832a771"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4d4542b-e41d-5aa5-b77f-61338768d4ed" :answer/id #uuid "c4d4542b-e41d-5aa5-b77f-61338768d4ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5aa0e64-7998-506a-b005-217cd2d97fd9" :answer/id #uuid "d5aa0e64-7998-506a-b005-217cd2d97fd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84aa4f2d-de88-5e30-8118-904ad76280e3" :answer/id #uuid "84aa4f2d-de88-5e30-8118-904ad76280e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19f056e4-3325-5f66-8071-2407f11d4bc8" :answer/id #uuid "19f056e4-3325-5f66-8071-2407f11d4bc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a1fe014-940d-5195-b2a9-07750832a771" :answer/id #uuid "3a1fe014-940d-5195-b2a9-07750832a771" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163289 :tutorial/content "For discrete random variables $X$  and  $Y$, the **conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$** is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X|Y=y]=\\sum_{x}x f_{X|Y}(x|y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f_{X|Y}(x|y)$ is the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given $Y.$ \n\nThis definition is similar to that of $\\textrm{E}[X].$ However, we now use the conditional PMF $f_{X|Y}(x|y)$ instead of the marginal PMF $f_X(x)$ in the summation.\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The conditional expectation $\\textrm E[X | Y = y]$ is (in general) a function of $y.$ This makes intuitive sense. If the distribution of $X$ varies with $Y,$ then the expected value of $X$ for a given $Y$ must vary with the value of $Y.$\n\n- If $y$ is replaced with a number, then $\\textrm E[X | Y = y]$ returns a single value.\n\n- If $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then $\\textrm E[X | Y = y] = \\textrm E[X]$ for all $y$. Again, this makes intuitive sense. If the outcome of $Y$ has no influence on the outcome of $X,$ then the distribution of $X$ and, consequently, its mean, is also unaffected by $Y.$\n\n- We sometimes use the notation $\\mu_{X|y}$ to denote $E[X | Y = y].$\n\nFinally, we have an analogous definition for $\\textrm E[Y|X=x]\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[Y|X=x]=\\sum_{y}y f_{Y|X}(y|x)\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162190 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
